// The Stonemason's stock in western Keldagrim.
//
// A thousand limestone bricks and twenty marble blocks, restocking a unit a minute (rate 100) -
// OSRS's own quantities for the two things this build has any use for.
//
// The PRICES are not here. ^poh_stone_sell is 500, a shop charges cost x multiplier / 1000, and
// both of these come out at exactly the OSRS price: 10 for a limestone brick and 125,000 for a
// marble block. Their cache costs are precisely twice what OSRS charges, which is what makes 500
// the honest number rather than a fitted one.
//
// GOLD LEAF was added when the gilded furniture arrived - the opulent rug and the gilded wall
// decoration are made of it. It is its own obj (poh_formal_mats.obj) rather than 377's unpriced
// In Search of the Myreque placeholder, and it is priced the same way the marble block is, coming
// out at OSRS's own 130,000.
//
// MAGIC STONES are stocked now. Nothing asked for one until the costume room's cape rack, whose
// top tier is a magic cape rack at level 99 and costs exactly one - which is what a magic stone is
// for in OSRS too. Five of them, restocking a unit every ten minutes (rate 1000), and priced the
// same way as the other three: OSRS's own 4,000,000.

[poh_stone_shop]
scope=shared
size=40
restock=yes
allstock=no
stackall=no
stock1=limestonebrick,1000,100
stock2=poh_marble_block,20,100
stock3=gold_leaf,20,100
stock4=magic_stone,5,1000
